+**⚠️ CRITICAL**: No user story work can begin until this phase is complete.
+
+**Note on scope**: `hash_password`/`password_matches` live here rather than in Phase 4 because they
+are part of the record's *encoding*, which is what `store` owns (plan.md → Structure Decision), and
+because `_validate_record` must validate what they write. Their requirement tests (FR-056, FR-061,
+FR-073) are in Phase 4, where the behaviour becomes observable.
+
+- [ ] T004 In `src/pastebin/store.py`, replace `RECORD_KEYS` with `REQUIRED_RECORD_KEYS = frozenset({"id", "content", "created_at", "expires_at", "delete_token"})` and `OPTIONAL_RECORD_KEYS = frozenset({"burn_after_reading", "password"})`.
+- [ ] T005 In `_validate_record` in `src/pastebin/store.py`, change the key-set rule: all five `REQUIRED_RECORD_KEYS` MUST be present, and any key outside `REQUIRED_RECORD_KEYS | OPTIONAL_RECORD_KEYS` makes the record damaged — so feature 001's extra-key rule and its `surprise`-key test still hold (FR-068). Keep the existing `StoreCorrupt` diagnostic naming the missing and unexpected keys. Depends on T004.
+- [ ] T006 In `_validate_record` in `src/pastebin/store.py`, add the `burn_after_reading` rule: absent is valid and means `False` (FR-067); when present it MUST be a boolean (`type(v) is bool`, so a `0`/`1` int is not accepted) or the record is damaged. Depends on T005.
+- [ ] T007 In `_validate_record` in `src/pastebin/store.py`, add the `password` rule per contracts/storage.md: absent or `null` means unprotected (FR-067); otherwise it MUST be an object with **exactly** the keys `iterations`, `salt`, `hash`, where `iterations` is an integer (`type(v) is int`, so a JSON boolean is not an integer here) and `> 0`, and `salt` and `hash` are each a non-empty, even-length, valid-hexadecimal string. Anything else is damaged (500, never 404). Depends on T006.
+- [ ] T008 Add `hash_password(password, iterations)` and `password_matches(password, stored)` to `src/pastebin/store.py`: derive with `hashlib.pbkdf2_hmac("sha256", password.encode("utf-8"), salt, iterations, dklen=32)` over a fresh `secrets.token_bytes(16)` salt, returning `{"iterations": int, "salt": <32 hex chars>, "hash": <64 hex chars>}`; verification re-derives with **the record's own** `salt` and `iterations` — never the current process's calibration — and compares with `secrets.compare_digest` on the derived bytes (FR-056, FR-061, FR-073). Add the `hashlib` import.
+- [ ] T009 Extend `create_paste` in `src/pastebin/store.py` to `create_paste(data_dir, content, expires_in=None, burn_after_reading=False, password=None, iterations=None)`: it **always** writes both new keys, so every record this version creates has the same seven-key shape — `"burn_after_reading": bool(...)` and `"password": None` when unprotected, or `hash_password(password, iterations)` when a plaintext password is given. The plaintext is used only to derive and is never stored, returned, or retained (FR-047, FR-056). Depends on T008.
+- [ ] T010 Add `_unlink_durably(data_dir, paste_id)` to `src/pastebin/store.py` implementing contracts/storage.md's removal protocol: `os.unlink(<DIR>/<id>.json)`, then `fd = os.open(<DIR>, os.O_RDONLY)` / `os.fsync(fd)` / `os.close(fd)`. Let `FileNotFoundError` propagate (something else removed it first); translate any other `OSError` from either call into `StoreCorrupt` (FR-048, FR-049).
+- [ ] T011 Reroute `delete_paste` in `src/pastebin/store.py` through `_unlink_durably`, so one durable-removal routine serves both the `DELETE` endpoint and the one-time claim. This strengthens FR-031 and changes nothing a caller can observe (FR-068). Depends on T010.
+
+**Checkpoint**: `python3 -m pytest` still fully green — the record now carries two keys that nothing
+yet sets, and removal is durable. User story work can begin.
