+## Phase 3: User Story 1 - Share something that disappears once it has been read (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP
+
+**Goal**: `"burn_after_reading": true` at publication makes a snippet's first successful read its
+last — the record is claimed atomically and durably *before* the response is written, so it is
+served exactly once and a restart cannot resurrect it.
+
+**Independent Test** (spec US1): Publish a snippet with the one-time option set, read it once through
+`GET /pastes/<id>` and confirm the text and metadata come back normally, then read it again and
+confirm 404. Repeat using `GET /pastes/<id>/raw` for the first read. Confirm an unread one-time
+snippet is still readable, still deletable with its delete token, and still subject to its expiry.
+
+### Tests for User Story 1 (write first; they MUST fail before T019–T021 land)
+
+- [ ] T012 [P] [US1] Create `tests/test_burn.py` with the publication tests on the `service` fixture: `test_fr045_burn_true_publishes`, `test_fr045_absent_burn_means_not_one_time`, `test_fr046_non_boolean_burn_is_400` parametrised over `"true"`, `"false"`, `1`, `0`, `None` (JSON `null`), `[]`, `{}` — no coercion, and `null` is a 400 rather than a decline (FR-046) — and `test_fr046_rejected_publication_creates_nothing` asserting the storage directory gained no file.
+- [ ] T013 [US1] Add the durability tests to `tests/test_burn.py`: `test_fr047_one_time_flag_is_on_disk` (via `service.read_record`, asserting `burn_after_reading is True`) and `test_fr047_one_time_survives_restart` (publish under `server_process`, stop, restart on the same `--data` directory, read once then 404).
+- [ ] T014 [US1] Add the consumption tests to `tests/test_burn.py`: `test_fr048_first_read_returns_then_404_forever` (first `GET` returns the full record, then both endpoints 404 repeatedly), `test_fr048_first_raw_read_returns_then_404` (first read through `/raw`, body exactly the text with no added newline, then 404 on both endpoints), `test_fr048_record_is_gone_when_the_read_returns` (`service.record_path(id)` does not exist the moment the 200 returns), `test_fr048_abandoned_response_still_consumes` (read the response headers over a raw socket, abandon the connection mid-body, then assert 404 — claim-before-send asserted by its consequence, research.md R-10).
+- [ ] T015 [US1] Add the no-consume tests to `tests/test_burn.py`: `test_fr049_expired_one_time_is_not_consumed` (hand-write a record whose `expires_at` has passed; 404, and the file is still present) and `test_fr049_damaged_one_time_is_not_consumed` (via `service.write_raw_record`; 500 plus a stderr diagnostic, and the file is still present).
+- [ ] T016 [US1] Add the exactly-once tests to `tests/test_burn.py`: `test_fr050_concurrent_reads_serve_exactly_one` — 16 threads released from a `threading.Barrier` onto the same unread one-time snippet on the `service` fixture, repeated over several trials, asserting exactly one 200 and fifteen 404s with no other status and no exception, and that the record file is gone — and `test_fr050_winner_body_is_complete`, asserting the single 200 carries the whole text, never a fragment.
+- [ ] T017 [US1] Add `test_fr051_consumed_snippet_stays_gone_across_restart` to `tests/test_burn.py`: publish and consume under `server_process`, stop the process, restart on the same directory, and assert 404 on both endpoints.
+- [ ] T018 [US1] Add the deletion and expiry interaction tests to `tests/test_burn.py`: `test_fr052_unread_one_time_deletes_with_token` (204, then 404), `test_fr052_consumed_one_time_delete_is_404`, and `test_fr053_expired_one_time_is_404_on_both_endpoints`.
+
+### Implementation for User Story 1
+
+- [ ] T019 [US1] Add `burn_paste(data_dir, paste_id)` to `src/pastebin/store.py`: call `_unlink_durably` and return `True` when this caller claimed the snippet, `False` on `FileNotFoundError` (a concurrent reader won), and let `StoreCorrupt` propagate for any other `OSError`. The boolean is *the* answer to "did I claim it", not a stand-in for a record (Constitution Principle II). Depends on T010.
+- [ ] T020 [US1] In `_publish` in `src/pastebin/server.py`, validate the new field: test membership with `"burn_after_reading" in payload` (absence, **not** `null`, is how a caller declines), require `type(value) is bool`, and otherwise send `400` with `'burn_after_reading' must be true or false`; pass the value through to `store.create_paste`. Depends on T009.
+- [ ] T021 [US1] In `_read` in `src/pastebin/server.py`, insert the claim in research.md R-05's order: after `self._load(paste_id)` has returned a live record (404 if absent/expired, 500 if damaged) and the text has been taken into a local variable, if `record.get("burn_after_reading")` is true call `store.burn_paste` — `False` → `self._not_found()` and serve nothing; `store.StoreCorrupt` → `self._damaged(...)` (500) — and only then write the response, from the text held in memory. Applies to both the structured and the `/raw` branch. Depends on T019.
+
+**Checkpoint**: User Story 1 is fully functional and independently testable. `python3 -m pytest
+tests/test_burn.py` and the whole feature 001 suite both pass. **This is the MVP.**
